# FlyerBox routing (formerly PerchQR).
#
# ---- Domain moves: everything lands on https://flyerbox.net ----------------
# perchqr.com stays registered FOREVER: every printed QR code before the rename
# encodes perchqr.com/q/<id>, and these 301s keep the path (/:splat) and the
# query string (Netlify passes it through), so /q/<id> and the Flexmls sign-in
# return (/oauth/spark/callback?code=...&state=...) keep working.
# Requires flyerbox.net as the site's primary domain in Netlify, with
# perchqr.com, flyerbox.ai and the www. names added as domain aliases.
# These must stay ABOVE every other rule, and the "!" forces them even when a
# real file exists at the path.
http://perchqr.com/*        https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
https://perchqr.com/*       https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
http://www.perchqr.com/*    https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
https://www.perchqr.com/*   https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
http://flyerbox.ai/*        https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
https://flyerbox.ai/*       https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
http://www.flyerbox.ai/*    https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
https://www.flyerbox.ai/*   https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
https://www.flyerbox.net/*  https://flyerbox.net/:splat  301!
#
# Netlify checks for a real file/folder at the requested path BEFORE applying
# any rule below, so /assets/*, /favicon.ico, etc. are served directly and
# never reach these rewrites — only paths with no matching file fall through.
#
# These are 200 rewrites (the file changes, the browser's URL bar doesn't),
# which is why every page these rules point at uses ABSOLUTE asset/link paths
# instead of relative ones — see the comment at the top of assets/perch.js.

# QR redirector: /q/<qr_codes.id> -> resolves the code, logs the scan, and
# forwards to its stored destination. See site/q.html.
/q/:id           /q.html?id=:id       200

# Flexmls (Spark OIDC) sign-in return page — see site/oauth-callback.html.
# Registered with FBS as the key's Redirect URI (FBS allows only ONE per key),
# so this exact path must stay. The key still says perchqr.com, so Flexmls
# returns to perchqr.com/oauth/spark/callback; the 301s above carry code+state
# to flyerbox.net, where the agent's session lives. That works because the
# `state` is signed server-side (nothing is kept in the browser), and the
# token exchange still sends the registered perchqr.com URI (secret
# SPARK_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI). If FBS ever moves the key to flyerbox.net, change
# that secret to match.
/oauth/spark/callback  /oauth-callback.html  200

# Business-card page — Scott's account only (not a feature for other agents).
# Put a QR code on the card pointing at /scott-bird/card. See site/card.html.
/scott-bird/card /card.html          200

# Per-agent listing detail page: /<slug>/listing?id=<propertyId>
/:slug/listing   /listing.html        200

# Admin panel — /app is the generic entry point (works for anyone who signs
# in, regardless of slug); /<slug>/access is the same page reached by a
# personalized, memorable link. app.html reads the slug out of the URL for
# the owner's benefit (auto-selects that agent in the switcher); a regular
# agent's own login already shows their own data either way.
/app             /app.html            200
/:slug/access    /app.html            200

# Administrator-only gate — deliberately not linked anywhere on the public
# site. Signs in against the same Supabase Auth pool as everyone else, but
# rejects any account that isn't PERCHQR_OWNER_ID before it can reach /app.
/admin           /admin.html          200

# Self-serve signup.
/signup          /signup.html         200

# TODO: the other reserved words in PLANNING.md's "Tenant URL shape" list
# (admin, api, www, login, signin, …) don't have real pages yet, so they're
# not routed here — but they're still blocked from being CLAIMED as a slug
# (enforced in supabase/schema.sql's agents_slug_not_reserved constraint, not
# just client-side). If a page is ever built for one of them, add its
# explicit rule here, above the catch-all below.

# Per-agent homepage — MUST stay last, since it matches any single path
# segment that isn't a real file and isn't matched by a rule above.
/:slug           /index.html          200
